# Kindred Editorial Database

Kindred is **not** a consumer of Foursquare, Google, or Yelp.
Provider APIs are **discovery tools**. The **Kindred Editorial Database** is the source of truth.

```
Provider APIs → Discovery Pipeline → Kindred Editorial Database → Editorial Ranking → Daily Newspaper
```

## Philosophy

- Once a restaurant is discovered, Kindred **owns** the editorial record.
- Each venue has a **permanent Kindred ID** (`food_drink_catalog.id` UUID).
- **Never blind-overwrite** provider data — merge via Source Manager with confidence scores.
- **Nothing is permanently deleted** — closed venues are archived for historical editions.
- Adding a provider = wiring another **importer** into the same Kindred record.

## Venue record

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| Kindred ID | Permanent UUID — never changes |
| Name, address, coordinates, website, phone | Resolved via Source Manager |
| Cuisine, editorial categories, editorial tags | Kindred-verified taxonomy |
| Editorial teaser, editorial article | Kindred editorial desk |
| Opening hours, price level, photos | Merged from providers + licensed sources |
| Confidence score (0–100) | Weighted aggregate of field provenance |
| Verification status | pending · verified · needs_review · rejected |
| Lifecycle | new → verified → featured → evergreen → needs_review → closed |
| field_sources | Per-field value, source, confidence, alternatives |
| source_history | Append-only merge audit trail |

## Source Manager

Every field knows where it came from. Trust tiers (highest wins on conflict):

| Source | Default confidence |
| --- | --- |
| Official Website | 99 |
| Kindred | 98 |
| Michelin / James Beard | 95 |
| Licensed photo | 90 |
| Google Places | 85 |
| OpenTable / Resy | 82 |
| Foursquare | 75 |
| Yelp | 70 |
| Community correction | 60 |

Implementation: `lib/edition/sourceManager.ts` · `places/venueImporter.ts`

## Editorial lifecycle

```
NEW → Verified → Featured → Evergreen → Needs Review → Closed
```

- **NEW** — discovered, not yet publish-ready
- **Verified** — passes confidence threshold; eligible for guide
- **Featured / Evergreen** — editorial promotions (manual; sync never auto-demotes)
- **Needs Review** — confidence dropped or missing from full sync — **not removed**
- **Closed** — archived; historical links keep working

Guide eligibility: `verified`, `featured`, `evergreen` only.
Homepage featured 8: still **editor-curated** — never auto-promote because a venue is new.

## Confidence thresholds

| Score | Action |
| --- | --- |
| ≥ 70 | Eligible for Food & Drink guide (`verified`) |
| < 50 | Mark `needs_review` — do not remove |
| Rejected discovery | `rejected` lifecycle — never published |

## Multi-provider links

`kindred_venue_provider_links` maps external IDs (Foursquare, Google, Yelp, …) to one Kindred venue.
Future importers merge observations into the same record — no duplicates.

## Cost controls (unchanged)

- Foursquare / Google / Yelp **never** called per user or session
- Shared metro catalog + scheduled incremental / full sync
- Skip unchanged records; regenerate editorial only on material change

## Editorial Score (venue recommendation strength)

Separate from verification confidence, provider ratings, and review counts.

| Field | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `editorial_score` | 0–100 — "Would the desk recommend this?" |
| `editorial_labels` | Structured tags (`editors_pick`, `hidden_gem`, …) |
| `editorial_reason` | Internal scoring explanation (not reader-facing) |
| `editorial_lock` | Manual override — sync updates facts only |

Implementation: `venueEditorialScore.ts` · `venueEditorialScoring.ts`

**Tiers:** 90+ signature · 80+ strong · 70+ useful · 60+ guide eligible · below 60 needs review

**Homepage:** `selectHomepageRecommendationCards()` — editorial score + daily rotation, still exactly 8 diverse picks.

**Guide:** `organizeFoodDrinkGuide()` — sort by editorial score within categories.

